{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/589800-vitae-and-mortals","id":589800,"title":"Vitae and mortals","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-13T19:39:13-07:00","id":589800,"title":"Vitae and mortals","content":"So, my ST is a story person, not a system person. We were discussing a particular NPC of hers (Molly) and the options we see for the character regarding my character. My Mekhet (Charles) is intrigued why two sleeping sips of Vitae didn't seem to faze Molly when they eventually &quot;met.&quot; The ST admitted later that Molly is Unbondable. Fair enough. I asked if a) she would still feel the addiction of the blood, and b) if she could be ghouled. The ST suggested I throw it out on the forum. <br /> <br /> My thought is that they are 3 different but related effects of the blood; I would expect that addiction might still be an issue, and that ghouling is about Charles' effort rather than Molly's resistance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T19:53:47-07:00","id":589824,"title":"","content":"I'd say addiction should definitely be an issue. <br /> <br /> Ghouling is more up in the air. There seems to be a certain bond between the ghoul and the regnant, the one who creates the ghoul. They get access to the disciplines of that vampire, which seems to suggest some personal connection that might be blocked by being Unbondable. For story purposes, I'd certainly allow Molly to be ghouled, as it makes everything more dangerous for those involved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T20:22:01-07:00","id":589831,"title":"","content":"Depends on why she's unbondable. Why reduce it to even three binary switches? It might be the property of any number of possible states that interact with these effects in different ways. Which is to say: the question &quot;is it possible to be immune to the Vinculum but subject to ghouling?&quot; is less interesting than the question &quot;what is it about Molly that protects her from the Vinculum, and how would that interact with ghouling?&quot;<br /> <br /> If your Storyteller has an idea in mind to explain Molly, or thinking about it presents an idea, great! You've given him some rope to hang you with. In the fun way!<br /> <br /> If you don't have ideas off the top of your head, go the other direction. Decide what would be more interesting to play out and then reverse-engineer what kind of interesting state would cause that result.<br /> <br /> As a general rule I'd scrap addiction if the Vinculum is out, personally. Most (but not all) of the stories of blood addiction play into similar arcs as those of the blood bond, and the story implied by the ability to resist the blood bond (either something inimical to vampirism or simply extraordinary self-control and security of self) probably benefits from keeping addiction out too. Ghouling may be another story, however.<br /> <br /> Some possibilities, limited by the lack of knowledge of who Molly is and what role she plays in your game:<ul><li>Molly <i>is</i> bonded. Just not to you. You think you were the first vamp to come up with that idea?</li> <li>Molly <i>is</i> bonded. To you. But that's not Molly.</li> <li>Something is watching over Molly, something nursing an old grudge with the Kindred.</li> <li>Molly is faint and hollow; the Life dissolves too thinly within her to sway her. (No addiction, either no ghouling or ghouling confers fewer benefits to her and a weaker tie to you than normal.)</li> <li>The opposite: Molly is vibrant and the purity of her lifeblood burns out the sludge of Vitae. (No addiction, no ghouling, and you probably don't want to find out what happens if you touch her blood, let alone drink it.)</li> <li>Molly comes from familial stock that has been influenced by the presence of Kindred, perhaps a distant relative of a ghoul dynasty, or residents of a domain under blood thralldom such as the clouds cast on parts of Hungary by the Csalad bloodline and their Lithopedia. (No or weaker addiction, but ghoulable and possibly deriving more benefits from it. Might be prone, if killed, to rising as a revenant or a spontaneous Embrace.)</li> <li>Something in Molly's diet has supernatural properties that inhibit the Vitae taking hold. She's been eating it for awhile. It lives within her, now. (Could be ghoulable, could not. Either way, this one implies strange side effects, possible dangers, or the production of a ghoul with some distinctly unghoulish traits.)</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T03:56:16-07:00","id":590080,"title":"","content":"If I were going for a mundane explanation as for why she's unbondable and can't become addicted to vitae, I'd say she has a medical condition like dysgeusia. <br /> <br /> If I were going for a more exotic reason, I'd say she's not human, she just looks human and shows up as human under the standard gamut of detection powers possessed by other supernatural types. (Only highly specific powers or circumstances will register what she really is.) She might even think she's human but she's not. (Like Dawn in Buffy the Vampire Slayer.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T06:51:40-07:00","id":590179,"title":"","content":"She should probably have the &quot;Weak Bonds&quot; merit from B&amp;S Ghoul section. Basically, it means she doesn't care for vincullum as much, but is still susceptible to Addiction <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> When I wanted such a character, I had her Resolve high (to resist addiction), and gave her the said merit (so that Vincullum is weaker.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T08:31:36-07:00","id":590237,"title":"","content":"I know the meta reason: She wanted Charles to have to work harder and more cleverly when dealing with Molly. The in-game reason, I'm not sure -- she has some bloodline connection with some kind of supernatural critter, but I'm not clear on the connection or what the critter is. The ST insists the NPC is human, just not swayed by the Vinculum. Ghouling would be really nice down the road; blood addiction has pluses and minuses to it. I may recommend she not include it just to make things simpler.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T08:43:42-07:00","id":590242,"title":"","content":"Addiction and blood bonding are certainly separate effects. Elder vampires are immune to the former, but not the latter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T06:21:45-07:00","id":591212,"title":"","content":"Thanks for all the replies. I pointed the ST to this thread and got this back:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Loserman has some clever ideas. He's on the right track. What IS it about Molly that makes her unbondable? <br /> She is not a ghoul. She herself is not any kind of superntural critter. Clearly she is human--tasting the blood and your observations tell you that. She carried and bore a child. She was injured in an accident and had no sort of 'supernatural recovery.' (Her wounds were internal--no head trauma or damage to her hands--so why did she quit being a surgeon?) She had to recover like any normal human. But there is certainly something a little different about her. <br /> <br /> The addiction factor is not clear. She might well be ghoulable. You have to figure out how to test these ideas. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}